==Old English==
===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*tīwa-'', from Indo-European ''*dhyeu-'' ‘god’.  Cognate with Old Norse [[Tyr|Týr]], Old High German [[Zio|Zīo]], Gothic [[𐍄𐌴𐌶]].  The IE root is also the source of Greek [[Ζευς]], Latin [[deus]], Hittite {{term|sc=Cuneiform|𒅆𒍑|tr=sius|lang=hit}}, Common Slavic ''*divъ'' (Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|дивъ|tr=divŭ|lang=cu}}).

